### Description

Create the fast macOS command-line harness target that hosts ReluxTunnelCore components for packet, SSH, relay, fault-injection, and metric experiments without requiring a Network Extension lifecycle for every iteration.
### Scope

In scope: CLI target and stable subcommand registry; structured configuration input; dependency injection; cancellation and signal handling; privacy-safe structured metrics output; deterministic seed and run metadata; temporary-resource cleanup; extension-equivalent core composition. Out of scope: implementing packet bridge or SSH commands, product profile UX, privileged networking, production credentials, and behavior that cannot later run inside the provider.
### Acceptance Criteria

1. ReluxTunnelHarness builds via SPM as a standalone macOS executable (NO generated Xcode/Tuist workspace required — that workspace is gated behind Gate A0/P0) and links the same ReluxTunnelCore products intended for the providers. 2. A no-op smoke command records source revision, dependency revisions, configuration, duration, platform, and metric schema in deterministic machine-readable output. 3. Signal cancellation and normal exit release temporary files, sockets, and tasks with tested exit codes. 4. Subcommands can inject clocks, transports, packet endpoints, pressure signals, and fault policies without importing app UI. 5. Swift Testing covers argument validation, result-schema versioning, cancellation, and cleanup.

## Instructions

The following instructions have been attached to this task:

### TASK-260715-pmww4f_spm-harness.md
> SPM-based harness constraints

Build ReluxTunnelHarness as an SPM executable target in this repo Package.swift (STANDALONE — NO generated Tuist workspace; that workspace is gated behind Gate A0/P0 and must NOT be a prerequisite here, per the ADR-011 SPM-harness-in-parallel decoupling). Link ReluxTunnelCore (the same library the providers use). Per .spec (ADR-011, platform-distribution.md ReluxTunnelHarness = macOS CLI for fast packet/SSH/relay experiments): provide injection seams (clocks, transports, packet endpoints, pressure signals, fault policies) for the upcoming packet-bridge (TASK-260715-3o0co4), HEV (1vv52g), and SSH (1af33i/1ozsb6) spikes, WITHOUT importing app UI or NetworkExtension. Deterministic machine-readable smoke output (source+dependency revisions, config, duration, platform, metric schema); tested signal-cancellation + normal-exit cleanup of temp files/sockets/tasks; Swift Testing for arg validation, result-schema versioning, cancellation, cleanup. Build + test must pass via swift build / swift test on macOS.




